The detector implementations acknowledge the following work and source references:

Jecmen et al., A Dataset on Malicious Paper Bidding in Peer Review (WWW 2023).
https://github.com/sjecmen/malicious_bidding_dataset

Jecmen et al., On the Detection of Reviewer-Author Collusion Rings From Paper Bidding.
https://github.com/sjecmen/peer-review-collusion-detection

The included evaluation code implements Counting, Pairwise Reciprocity,
Low-rank Residual, OQC, TellTail, greedy densest, and Fraudar for CABAL inputs.
TellTail and Fraudar additionally draw on the methods of Hooi et al.
The CABAL ports include adaptations for multiple-paper authorship, bid encoding,
random starts and tie handling, and a Charikar approximation for densest subgraph.
Upstream datasets and researcher publication portfolios are not bundled.
